1
00:00:00,104 --> 00:00:01,510
(Q11（单选）) Hello, I'm Hayden.

2
00:00:01,510 --> 00:00:06,213
I'm one of the archaeologists investigating the site here at Bidcaster.

3
00:00:06,213 --> 00:00:13,369
This is the third summer for this community project, and most of the people digging here are volunteers.

4
00:00:13,369 --> 00:00:25,013
[Q11答案句（B） set up = start， up and down the country = national + Q11干扰项C] I'm a full-time archaeologist for the town council, but I was asked to join the project by NHA, a charity which sets up projects like this up and down the country.

5
00:00:25,013 --> 00:00:33,209
As you can see, we're next to Bidcaster Castle, which is great because the owners let us use their facilities.

6
00:00:33,209 --> 00:00:36,822
(Q12) So, how did we get to where we are today?

7
00:00:36,822 --> 00:00:46,103
Many archaeology projects happen when an ancient object is found, and in our case, that object was a gold coin.

8
00:00:46,103 --> 00:00:59,502
[Q12干扰项C/B。 并列关系 排除。 + are often found 不是 题目中所指的coin] Coins are often found by people using metal detectors to look for things buried in the ground – or coins are uncovered when wild animals like rabbits have been digging tunnels.

9
00:00:59,502 --> 00:01:07,266
[Q12答案句（A） heavy rain = rainstorm] Here, a walker found it on the ground after a rainstorm washed away some of the earth and sand.

10
00:01:07,266 --> 00:01:21,084
(Q13) When the story of the gold coin hit the news, Peter Swift, an amateur historian, contacted me to say he believed there had been a village on this site, centuries before the castle was built.

11
00:01:21,084 --> 00:01:37,137
[Q13答案句： by chance = lucky 平行替换， 500-hundred-year-old = old  解释型， maps and documents = record(n.)] Just by chance, the team found some old maps and documents in our library which showed five-hundred-year-old drawings of ruined buildings on the grassy area between the outer stone walls of the castle and the river.

12
00:01:37,137 --> 00:01:40,444
We knew then we were onto something.

13
00:01:40,444 --> 00:01:49,864
(Q14) [Q14干扰项（A） have found] Over the three summers the team has been here, we've found the remains of several buildings, and more broken pots than you can count!

14
00:01:49,864 --> 00:01:58,013
[Q14答案句（C） still waiting = hope to, brooches and other jewelry = jewellery 上下义] Normally you'd expect to find brooches and other jewellery, but we're still waiting to uncover any such items.

15
00:01:58,013 --> 00:02:06,811
[Q14干扰项（B） 现在已经发现了。 时态不符，] The people who once lived here were skilled at making tools from animal bones, as you'll see when you visit the exhibition.

16
00:02:06,811 --> 00:02:21,832
(Q15) [Q15答案句（B） outline = border + Q15干扰项（C） 排除依据： 否定信号词 no other ...] Besides the discovery of the village, we've also found evidence of human activity on the other side of the river – no other houses or huts so far, but we can see the borders of an ancient field system.

17
00:02:21,832 --> 00:02:29,947
[Q15干扰项A： 排除依据， 否定信号词 but it turned out to be] At one point we found a long wall and thought it was an ancient palace, but it turned out to be a modern wall.

18
00:02:29,947 --> 00:02:35,223
(Q16) This summer's work will end soon, but we'll be back next summer.

19
00:02:35,223 --> 00:02:42,010
[Q16答案句（C） put on 举办 组织= organize] In the meantime, we're putting on a series of guided tours for school groups this autumn.

20
00:02:42,010 --> 00:02:46,853
[Q16干扰项（B） 时态不符， saw] Oh and, maybe you saw the TV documentary about our project.

21
00:02:46,853 --> 00:02:54,617
[Q16干扰项（A）排除依据： 否定 - not sure] That suggested the objects we've found are going to the town's museum, but we don't know that for sure yet.

22
00:02:54,617 --> 00:03:00,209
(Q17（地图）) When you enter the site, please make sure you keep to the paths at all times.

23
00:03:00,209 --> 00:03:06,456
There are a few other things – the highlights of the site, if you like – that I want to mention.

24
00:03:06,456 --> 00:03:12,533
Take a look at the map; our present location is marked at the bottom.

25
00:03:12,533 --> 00:03:18,038
This year we've identified the foundations of an ancient bridge.

26
00:03:18,038 --> 00:03:25,044
And it's really exciting today because a team of divers are in the river searching for lost objects.

27
00:03:25,044 --> 00:03:35,056
To reach the bridge, take the main path ahead of you, go straight on and keep going till the path bends to the left.

28
00:03:35,056 --> 00:03:39,221
You'll see a smaller track leading off to the right.

29
00:03:39,221 --> 00:03:43,586
Follow that to take you to the river, where the divers are.

30
00:03:43,586 --> 00:03:47,219
(Q18) You might be interested to see the rubbish pit.

31
00:03:47,219 --> 00:03:52,889
This is very near the castle walls in the northwest corner of the site.

32
00:03:52,889 --> 00:03:58,655
It actually dates to the time of the castle and not the ancient village.

33
00:03:58,655 --> 00:04:06,836
We found oyster shells and fish bones, and we assume they were thrown from the castle kitchen above.

34
00:04:06,836 --> 00:04:12,842
(Q19) One area we excavated in the first summer uncovered the site of a meeting hall.

35
00:04:12,842 --> 00:04:21,288
We knew it was an important building because it had two rows of post holes, deep enough to support a large roof.

36
00:04:21,288 --> 00:04:28,800
It's the largest structure in the central area of the site, next to the current excavation area.

37
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:33,298
(Q20) Last year we discovered a fish pond in the ancient village.

38
00:04:33,298 --> 00:04:36,024
Normally these were beside a river.

39
00:04:36,024 --> 00:04:42,358
The pond here is further away, but it's possible the river has moved slightly.

40
00:04:42,358 --> 00:04:52,834
Anyway, to get there from here, you turn right at the first information board you come to, and follow the path into the trees.

41
00:04:52,834 --> 00:04:56,958
Before you come out of the trees, you'll see it on your right.

42
00:04:56,958 --> 00:05:01,201
If you reach the river, you've gone too far.

43
00:05:01,201 --> 00:05:03,701
So, does anyone …

